# PART 8 — DIGITAL PDF READER

Build a professional PDF reader.

The reader is a central feature of this platform.

### Reader features
- Display PDF documents using PDF.js.
- Page navigation.
- Previous and next page.
- Page number indicator.
- Zoom in and out.
- Fit-to-width.
- Fit-to-page.
- Fullscreen mode.
- Search inside the document where supported.
- Reading progress.
- Continue from last position.
- Bookmarks.
- Reading history.
- Responsive mobile reading.
- Loading and document error states.

### Access rules

Free books:
- Can be read according to their published access settings.

Paid books:
- Can only be read by customers with a valid, verified entitlement.

The frontend must never be the authority deciding whether a paid book can be opened.

### PDF security

- Keep original PDF files in a private Supabase Storage bucket.
- Never expose permanent public URLs for paid PDFs.
- Verify the authenticated customer on the server.
- Verify book availability and entitlement before issuing access.
- Use short-lived signed access URLs or protected streaming.
- Revoke or expire access according to the security design.
- Prevent direct unauthenticated access to paid files.
- Apply user-specific watermarking where technically appropriate and configurable.
- Do not claim that browser-based PDF access can prevent every screenshot or copy.

Do not unlock paid books based on a browser-side payment flag.

