- purchases
- entitlements
- reading_progress
- bookmarks
- reading_history
- notifications
- reviews where enabled
- admin_activity_logs
- site_settings
- homepage_sections where appropriate

Use:
- Primary keys.
- Foreign keys.
- Unique constraints.
- Appropriate indexes.
- Timestamps.
- Data integrity rules.
- Database migrations.
- Safe transactional operations.

Do not create unnecessary duplicate sources of truth.

### Important business relationships

- One customer can have many orders.
- One order can contain one or more books.
- One order can have payment attempts or payment events.
- A verified successful purchase creates or activates the appropriate entitlement.
- An entitlement determines whether a customer can access a paid book.
- Reading progress belongs to the correct customer and book.
- Wishlist items belong to the correct customer.

Use database transactions or carefully designed server-side atomic operations for critical purchase and entitlement changes.

