# PART 13 — DATABASE SECURITY AND RLS

Enable and properly configure Supabase Row Level Security.

Policies must enforce real ownership and authorization.

Examples:
- Customers can read and update only their own permitted profile information.
- Customers can read their own orders.
- Customers can read their own purchases and entitlements.
- Customers can manage their own wishlist.
- Customers can manage their own reading progress and bookmarks.
- Public users can only read published public book metadata.
- Public users cannot access private PDF files.
- Only authorized administrators can manage books, categories, pricing, and settings.
- Only trusted server-side operations can create verified payment records and entitlements.

Do not use `auth.role() = 'authenticated'` as proof that someone is an administrator.

Use a secure, server-verifiable role strategy.

Test the policies with:
- Anonymous user.
- Normal customer.
- Different customer.
- Administrator.

Never expose the Supabase service-role key to the browser.

